// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
row('blend(a,b,gap) / loft: BlendFeature targets[2]; gap sets sketch b offset = offset(a) + gap; no numbers stored on the feature itself', 'unsupported',
  `ROLL-UP = worst SOLID sub-case through the guarded rig; the stale lesson text and the oracle-reliability row are documentation/oracle defects, not solids, and are excluded. The ordinary case is exact (parity fixture 40x40 -> 10x10 gap 30: OCCT = brep-rs = truck = closed form 21000.0000, dVol ${f(g1('rect-rect-parity').dTO)}, faces 6/6/6). RAW: every class in rows 14-33 whose RAW line shows a build puts a wrong or unverifiable solid in front of the student with no sentence. GUARDED: ${enfTxt} UNSUPPORTED (not refused, no acceptable sentence) are only the two script-layer sentences the guard cannot reach because runScript halts before a doc exists: extra arguments ("was ignored" is false) and bad arguments spelled loft() (sentence says blend()); fixing them needs packages/script, which is read-only here. Data model confirmed by runScript: sketch('top',5).rect(40,40); sketch('top').rect(10,10); blend(a,b,30) gives [sk1 xy offset 5, sk2 xy offset 35, bl1 {id,kind,targets:[sk1,sk2]}] (feature has no number); blend(a,b,-30) with a at offset 40 gives sk2 offset 10 and targets [sk2,sk1] (bottom first), toScript re-emits loft(sk2, sk1, 30). ENFORCEMENT JSON: see top-level "enforcement".`);

row('blend between two different outlines (rect to circle, rect to rect of another size, polygon sections), ruled loft', 'refused',
  `ROLL-UP (worst sub-case through the guarded rig = refused with a plain sentence). SUPPORTED (S1-S5, exact): parallel-sided same-count polygons incl. concave and any start corner/winding (${n7pass.length}+${n7hpass.length} fuzz pairs, 0 wrong), circle<->circle, regular 3/4/5/6/8-gon with a corner on +u <-> circle (<=2.0e-4), axis-aligned rectangle up to 2:1 <-> circle (<=1.1e-4), rounded rectangle up to 4:3 <-> circle (<=8.6e-5). REFUSED (RAW wrong): non-parallel sides, different corner counts incl. one redundant collinear point, polygon<->circle outside S3/S4, rounded outlines outside S5, unmatched start vertex, tied pairings. Rows below give each class with RAW numbers and the sentence.`,
  ['sides', 'count', 'circle-poly', 'arcs', 'start', 'tie'].map((c) => sentenceOf(c)).join(' | '));

// extra args (script layer) - N10 holds both spellings
const N10 = J.N10; const n10 = (name, call) => N10.find((r) => r.name === name && r.call === call);
const extra = ['(a, b, 30, 5);', "(a, b, 30, 'zzz');", '(a, b, 30, { height: 30 });', '(a, b, 30, 5, 6);', '(a, b, c, 30);'];
const extraCall = (name, tail) => N10.find((r) => r.name === name && r.call.endsWith(name + tail));
const after = n10('blend', 'blend(a, b, 30); const k = cuboid(5, 5, 5);');
row('blend needs exactly two sketches; extra arguments named and refused', 'unsupported',
  `RAW and GUARDED are the same here (the script halts in runScript before any doc exists, so the guard never runs). No solid is built, nothing reaches a kernel; but the SENTENCE IS NOT ACCEPTABLE, so this is not status refused: (1) it says the extra argument "was ignored", which is false: re-measured, the script stops (errors=1, no bl1 in the doc: ${N10.filter((r) => /, 30, (5|'zzz'|\{ height: 30 \}|5, 6)\);$/.test(r.call)).every((r) => !r.hasBlend && r.errors.length === 1)} for all ${N10.filter((r) => /, 30, (5|'zzz'|\{ height: 30 \}|5, 6)\);$/.test(r.call)).length} extra-argument calls) and nothing after it runs; (2) it says "blend()" when the student typed loft(): ${JSON.stringify(extraCall('loft', '(a, b, 30, 5);').errors[0])}; (3) three sketches, blend(a,b,c,30), is reported as "the fourth argument (30)", never "three sketches": ${JSON.stringify(extraCall('blend', '(a, b, c, 30);').errors[0])}. Shipped sentences (blend spelling): ${['(a, b, 30, 5);', "(a, b, 30, 'zzz');", '(a, b, 30, { height: 30 });', '(a, b, 30, 5, 6);'].map((t) => JSON.stringify(extraCall('blend', t).errors[0])).join(' | ')}. A valid blend(a,b,30) followed by cuboid(5,5,5) builds both (kinds ${after.kinds.join(',')}). Replacement that would pass (needs packages/script, read-only here; the shipped sentence is pinned by packages/script test/stray-args.test.mjs): "loft() takes two sketches and a gap, so it stopped before building anything; take out the extra argument (5) and run it again." For a ModelDoc that already holds N targets the guard does refuse with a plain sentence (rows "ModelDoc blend feature with 3 targets / 1 or 0 targets").`);

// bbox artifact
const bbp = ALL.filter((c) => !c.guard && c.dBbox !== undefined && c.kind === 'polygon'); const bbc = ALL.filter((c) => !c.guard && c.dBbox !== undefined && c.kind === 'curved');
const r1poly = R1raw.filter((r) => r.D?.truckBboxVsAnalyticSketch !== undefined && !/circle|round|arc|slot|geom/.test(r.src) && r.truck?.bbox);
const r1curv = R1raw.filter((r) => r.D?.truckBboxVsAnalyticSketch !== undefined && /circle|round|arc/.test(r.src) && r.truck?.bbox && !/slot|geom/.test(r.src));
