row('known referee artifact: bbox disagreement at about 1e-7 between truck loft and OCCT', 'supported',
  `Re-measured on the guard-passed cases: straight-sided ${bbp.length} cases, truck-vs-OCCT bbox disagreement max ${f(mx(bbp.map((c) => c.dBbox)))} (median 1.0e-7); circle/arc lofts ${bbc.length} cases, max ${f(mx(bbc.map((c) => c.dBbox)))} (median 1.0e-7). Which side owns it (round-1 raw, blend-loft.measure-results.json D): on ${r1poly.length} straight-sided scripts the truck bbox sits on the sketch corners to ${f(mx(r1poly.map((r) => r.D.truckBboxVsAnalyticSketch)))} while OCCT's BRepBndLib.AddOptimal box is ${f(mx(r1poly.map((r) => r.D.occtBboxVsAnalyticSketch)))} larger than the corners: the 1e-7 is OCCT's added tolerance. On ${r1curv.length} circle/arc scripts the truck box is up to ${f(mx(r1curv.map((r) => r.D.truckBboxVsAnalyticSketch)))} off the exact extent (tessellation), so for curved lofts the artifact is up to 9.2e-7 and is partly truck's. Neither changes a volume or a status; do not read a bbox below 1e-6 as a defect.`);

